{"id":8179421,"docketId":65277006,"caseName":"Linton v. Heye","caseNameFull":"Ph\u0153be R. E. E. Linton, in Error v. Fred Heye","slug":"linton-v-heye","docketNumber":"No. 508","dateFiled":"1904-04-11","dateArgued":null,"dateCertGranted":null,"year":1904,"scdbId":"","direction":"","votesMajority":null,"votesMinority":null,"disposition":"","posture":"","syllabus":null,"summary":null,"headnotes":null,"proceduralHistory":null,"attorneys":null,"natureOfSuit":"","citationCount":1,"judges":"","jurisdictionType":"","opinions":[{"id":8141336,"type":"majority","typeCode":"020lead","perCuriam":false,"author":"","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":1404,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"majority\">\n<p id=\"AZ1\">. In error to the Supreme Court of the State of Nebraska. Motions to dismiss or affirm submitted March 21,1904. Decided April 11, 1904. <em>Per Curiam. </em>Judgment affirmed with costs, on the authority of <em>Campbell </em>v. <em>Holt, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"91486\"><a href=\"/opinion/91486/campbell-v-holt/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Campbell v. Holt\">115 U. S. 620</a></span>; <em>Richardson </em>v. <em>Louisville and Nashville Railroad Company, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"94806\"><a href=\"/opinion/94806/richardson-v-louisville-nashville-railroad/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Richardson v. Louisville &amp; Nashville Railroad\">169 U. S. 128</a></span>; <em>Giles </em>v. <em>Little, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"92763\"><a href=\"/opinion/92763/giles-v-little/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Giles v. Little\">134 U. S. 645</a></span>. See <em>Lantry </em>v. <em>Wolff, </em>49 Nebraska, 374; <em>Murphy </em>v. <em>Evans Steam Laundry Company, </em>52 Nebraska, 593; <em>Linton </em>v. <em>Heye, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"6655351\"><a href=\"/opinion/6772382/linton-v-heye/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Linton v. Heye\">95 N. W. Rep. 1040</a></span>. <em>Mr. John C.